<newsitem itemid="180645" id="root" date="1996-11-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Charles Sidney year pretax profits up 56 pct.</title>
<headline>Charles Sidney year pretax profits up 56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to August 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  9.5		  vs   7.3</p>
<p> Pretax			 5.7		  vs   3.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   252.8		  vs 186.3</p>
<p> Operating profit	   8.2		  vs   5.0</p>
<p> Exceptional		 nil		   vs charge 1.1</p>
<p> Interest charge	    2.47		 vs   1.33</p>
<p> Tax			    1.77		 vs   1.21</p>
<p>NOTE - Charles Sidney Plc, a car and commercial vehicle dealership and rental operator, said that because of a change to its year end, the next report and accounts will be issued for the 16 months to December 1996.</p>
<p>It said a second interim dividend was not being paid but that a final dividend would be recommended at the time of announcing the results for the 16-month period.</p>
<p>It said that trading since August 31 had continued in line with expectations.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
